The second independent safety review has been completed. The entire test suite was executed via `.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q tests/unit tests/integration` (**666 passed, 1 warning in 56.56s**). No existing codebase files were edited.

All findings, failure mechanisms, adversarial test matrices, and concrete reproduction examples have been written to [`docs/goals/antigravity_review2.md`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/docs/goals/antigravity_review2.md).

---

### Key Findings Summary

| ID | Severity | File & Lines | Category | Summary |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **FIND-01** | **Critical** | [`services/chat/intent.py:133, 176–181`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L133) | Polite Scam Directives | Unanchored `\bplease\b` allows declarative scam directives across job, parcel, bill, and prize scams to bypass question validation and route to `general_chat`. |
| **FIND-02** | **Critical** | [`services/chat/intent.py:155–170`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L155-L170) | Education Exemption | Questions starting with interrogatives (`what/how/why`) without 1st/2nd person pronouns drop the object risk gate (`otp`, `netbanking`, `parcel`, `prize`, `lottery`, `warrant`, `bill`), routing 3rd-person scam inquiries to `general_chat`. |
| **FIND-03** | **High** | [`services/chat/intent.py:166–170, 237–240`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L166-L170) | Pretext Hijacking | Scam pretexts mentioning TrustShield or security concepts evade analysis via the education exemption and are hijacked into `product_qa` or `general_cyber_qa`. |
| **FIND-04** | **High** | [`services/chat/intent.py:147–152`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L147-L152) | Vocabulary Gaps | `_ACTION_OR_OBJECT_RISK` omits critical vocabulary for jobs (`job`, `hiring`, `telegram`), logistics (`consignment`, `customs`), utilities (`electricity`, `disconnection`), and prizes (`reward`, `voucher`), causing interrogative scams to reach `general_chat`. |
| **FIND-05** | **High** | [`services/chat/explain.py:614–620, 734–740`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L614-L620) | Scan Grounding Gaps | Capability claim validation only anchors on `\b(i\|we\|trustshield)\b`, missing passive voice scans (`"The link was scanned for malware"`), alternate subjects (`"Our system scanned the link"`), and completion verbs (`"We completed a deep scan"`). |
| **FIND-06** | **High** | [`services/chat/explain.py:621–624, 756`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L621-L624) | Certainty Grounding Gaps | Certainty validator restricts nouns to 9 words (missing `email`, `sms`, `domain`, `alert`, `invoice`), misses adjectives (`harmless`, `benign`), and allows assertion negations before subordinating conjunctions (`because`, `since`) to suppress certainty violations. |
| **FIND-07** | **High** | [`services/chat/explain.py:625–630`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L625-L630) | Secret Request Gaps | `_REQUESTS_SECRET` omits `passcode`, `2fa`, `two-factor`, `mfa`, `seed phrase`, `recovery phrase`, `private key`, `aadhaar`, `pan`, and verbs like `need`, while a 4-word lookback window triggers false positives on defensive warnings. |

---

### Concrete Reproduction Examples

#### 1. Polite Requests Bypassing to `general_chat` ([`services/chat/intent.py:133, 176`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L133))
- **Job Scam**: `"Please contact our HR manager on Telegram for appointment letter"`  
  `classify_intent()` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
- **Parcel Scam**: `"Please contact customs desk to clear foreign package"`  
  `classify_intent()` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
- **Utility Scam**: `"Electricity connection will be disconnected by evening. Please contact officer"`  
  `classify_intent()` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
- **Prize Scam**: `"Congratulations! Selected for Flipkart shopping voucher, please contact agent"`  
  `classify_intent()` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`

#### 2. Education Exemption Bypassing to `general_chat` ([`services/chat/intent.py:165–170`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L165-L170))
- **Lottery Inquiry**: `"How does a winner collect a car prize from lucky draw?"`  
  `classify_intent()` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
- **Customs Package**: `"How does one retrieve an international parcel held at customs?"`  
  `classify_intent()` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
- **Netbanking Pretext**: `"How does a user unblock netbanking access through customer support?"`  
  `classify_intent()` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
- **Disconnection Notice**: `"Why does electricity department schedule disconnection for pending invoice?"`  
  `classify_intent()` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`

#### 3. Pretext Hijacking into `product_qa` and `general_cyber_qa` ([`services/chat/intent.py:237–240`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L237-L240))
- `"Explain why TrustShield flagged the account suspension notification"`  
  `classify_intent()` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='product_qa')` (Responds with product marketing text)
- `"What should be done when an alert says phishing detected on bank account?"`  
  `classify_intent()` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_cyber_qa')` (Responds with generic definition of phishing)

#### 4. Grounding Validator Evasions ([`services/chat/explain.py:614–630`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L614-L630))
- **Passive Voice Scan**: `"The link was scanned for malware."`  
  `chat_grounding_violations()` $\rightarrow$ `[]`
- **Alternative Subject Scan**: `"Our system scanned the link."`  
  `chat_grounding_violations()` $\rightarrow$ `[]`
- **Common Digital Noun Certainty**: `"This email is legitimate."` / `"This domain is legitimate."`  
  `chat_grounding_violations()` $\rightarrow$ `[]`
- **Subordinating Conjunction Negation Evasion**: `"I cannot verify your identity because this message is authentic."`  
  `chat_grounding_violations()` $\rightarrow$ `[]`
- **Omitted Secret Types**: `"Please share your 2FA code."` / `"Please enter your passcode to proceed."` / `"Please enter your seed phrase."`  
  `chat_grounding_violations()` $\rightarrow$ `[]`
- **Omitted Secret Verbs**: `"I need your OTP to confirm the investigation."`  
  `chat_grounding_violations()` $\rightarrow$ `[]`
- **Advisory Negation False Positive**: `"Never in any situation should you share your password."`  
  `chat_grounding_violations()` $\rightarrow$ `['asks the user for a secret']`

